<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-HSBC Australia appoints new chief economist.</title>
<headline>RTRS-HSBC Australia appoints new chief economist.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>HSBC Markets has appointed John Edwards as chief economist for its treasury and capital market operations in Australia, the group said on Monday.</p>
<p>Edwards was senior economic adviser to former Prime Minister Paul Keating from 1991 to 1994. Since then he has worked as an adviser at Macquarie Bank and more recently as chief economist for Societe Generale Australia, HSBC said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
